    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98">

                <pb facs="0112" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense(M)/11927: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Scotten</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-02-08T12:00:00-06:00">February 8,
                        1943—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 3:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>99. Referring to my telegram No. 94, February 5, 11 a.m.<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d98-f1"/> I am in receipt of a letter<anchor n="15" xml:id="d98-f2"
                    /> from the Minister of Agriculture<anchor n="16" xml:id="d98-f3"/> stating that
                    the President<anchor n="17" xml:id="d98-f4"/> is in principle in complete accord
                    with the Memorandum of Understanding. The Minister adds that his Ministry will
                    take great pleasure in cooperating in every way with the survey party which he
                    trusts will come as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>The Minister and I went over the Memorandum of Understanding this morning and he
                    suggested certain minor changes which I will submit by airgram for the
                    Department’s consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Scotten</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
